PROCESS-ALIGNMENT.md

# --- working artefacts, never part of the project ---------------------------
# _TO-DELETE is a quarantine folder (nothing here is ever `rm`'d, it is moved
# here for review). A single `git add -A` would otherwise publish a directory
# literally named "_TO-DELETE" on a repo used for job applications -- so its
# CONTENTS stay ignored via the wildcard below, never the directory itself.
#
# rule://quarantine's own LEDGER.jsonl is the one exception: "the record IS
# the recovery" for a Tier 1 purge, where the bytes are already gone -- a
# ledger git never tracks is exactly as deletable as what it records. `!`
# only works if git can still descend into the directory to find it, which
# `_TO-DELETE/` (the directory itself, ignored as one atomic unit) does not
# allow -- `_TO-DELETE/*` (its immediate contents) does.
# A middle slash anchors a gitignore pattern to this file's own directory
# (the repo root) -- `_TO-DELETE/*` alone would stop matching
# `test/_TO-DELETE/...` (test/mutate.test.ts's own scratch backups use that
# exact nested path), which the prior, unanchored `_TO-DELETE/` pattern DID
# still ignore. `**/` restores "any depth" for the contents; the negation
# stays anchored with a leading `/` so ONLY the root quarantine folder's own
# ledger is ever tracked, never a same-named ledger nested elsewhere.
**/_TO-DELETE/*
!/_TO-DELETE/LEDGER.jsonl
.shots/
restore_landmasses.py
test-results/
public/.arterial-network-data.json
# test/originStability.test.ts's own disposable public/ copy -- created
# under the repo root (not the OS tmpdir) so it can resolve npm packages
# via repoRoot/node_modules; cleaned up in a `finally` block on a normal
# run, but a killed run could leave one behind.
/origin-stability-*/
